sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on the major straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth the fourth binomial.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a major straight line divided at {C}, so that {AC} is greater than {CB}, let {DE} be a rational straight line, and to {DE} let there be applied the parallelogram {DF|DFh} equal to the square on {AB} and producing {DG} as its breadth.

I say that {DG} is a fourth binomial straight line.

Make the same construction as shown before.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="200" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.63 diagram" src="propX60.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (X.60's): the major AB divided at C, the rational DE,
    // and DF (EDGF) equal to the square on AB applied to DE with breadth DG;
    // inside it DH (EDKH) equal to the square on AC, KL (HKML) equal to the
    // square on CB, the remainder MF, and NO through the midpoint N of MG.
    // "Make the same construction as shown before" is one slide that builds
    // DH, KL, N and NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: a solid twin DE (initiallyHidden) so the
    // rational line strokes before DF is applied; transparent targets AC,
    // CB, DG, DM, MG, DK, KM, MN, ML (;0;0;0); a faceless twin DFh of the
    // random-faced EDGF, which would be raised over DH and KL when lit
    // (#140), reached as {DF|DFh}; faceless targets DL (D,M,L,E) and MF
    // (M,G,F,L). No angle is called right in the text, so no markers.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D, E (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. D and E arrive with "let DE be a rational
    // straight line", so both are deferred. G, F, K, H, M, L, N, O are
